Third-Party Licenses
====================

This file lists the license of every third-party Python package installed in this project's
environment, as declared by each package's own distribution metadata. Generated 2026-07-27
(Session 190) via a live scan of `importlib.metadata` across all installed distributions,
cross-checked against each package's PyPI license classifiers; refreshed 2026-07-27 (Session 191)
after `python-gitlab` was dropped in Phase 1 of `docs/planning/httpx-adapter-migration.md`.
Re-run after any dependency change:

    uv run python3 -c "
    import importlib.metadata as m
    for d in sorted(m.distributions(), key=lambda d: d.metadata['Name'].lower()):
        print(d.metadata['Name'], d.metadata['Version'], d.metadata.get('License-Expression') or d.metadata.get('License'))
    "

This project's own two packages (`model-project-constructor`, `model-project-constructor-data-agent`)
are included for completeness; they are not third-party.

Summary
-------

- **95 installed distributions** (was 96 — `python-gitlab` removed Session 191, Phase 1 of the
  httpx adapter migration).
- **Zero GPL-only, zero AGPL** dependencies.
- **One LGPL-3.0 direct dependency: `PyGithub`** (see below). Until Session 191, `python-gitlab`
  was a second LGPL-3.0 direct dependency (GitLab adapter) — removed when the GitLab adapter was
  rewritten against direct `httpx` calls (`docs/planning/httpx-adapter-migration.md` Phase 1).
  `PyGithub` remains pending Phase 2 of that plan.
- **Three MPL-2.0 components** (one direct-ish via a first-party dependency's own dependency
  tree; see notes): `certifi`, `orjson`, `pathspec`.
- Everything else is MIT, BSD (2- or 3-clause), Apache-2.0, ISC, or PSF-2.0 — all permissive.

Copyleft and weak-copyleft dependencies (read first)
-----------------------------------------------------

| Package | Version | License | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| `PyGithub` | 2.9.1 | LGPL-3.0-only | GitHub adapter (`agents/website` repo-host layer). The PyPI classifier is version-ambiguous ("GNU Library or Lesser General Public License (LGPL)"); the bundled `licenses/COPYING.LESSER` text is GNU LGPL **version 3** with no "or later" clause, so this project treats it as LGPL-3.0-only. Pending removal in Phase 2 of `docs/planning/httpx-adapter-migration.md`. |
| `certifi` | 2026.2.25 | MPL-2.0 | Transitive, via `httpx`/`anthropic`. |
| `orjson` | 3.11.8 | MPL-2.0 AND (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) | Transitive, via `langgraph`. |
| `pathspec` | 1.0.4 | MPL-2.0 | Transitive, via `mkdocs`/`hatchling` (docs/build tooling only, not shipped in the runtime application). |

LGPL compliance note: `PyGithub` is used purely through its public Python API (no source
modification, no static linking) — LGPL §4/§6 compliance is satisfied by Python's import
mechanism, which already permits re-linking against a modified version of the library. The GitLab
adapter no longer uses an LGPL SDK as of Session 191 (direct `httpx` calls). See
`docs/wiki/claims-model-starter/Security-Considerations.md` §9 for how each adapter is used.

